From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:19:47 +0900
Subject: Scene: windows covered by one opaque window over the whole output
 get frame callbacks once a second
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A window whose opaque region covers an entire output (a fullscreen view, our floating window in
fullscreen) hides every window below it there, and the occlusion culling already paints none of
them. They still got a frame callback with every frame of the output, and each of their commits
scheduled one: a program animating behind kept the output compositing identical frames at full
rate (on the phone ~70 handed to Android per second).

Per output, the frame now finds the topmost window that the occlusion culling would let cover the
whole output (not translucent, not transformed, untransformed screen) and marks the windows below
it that lie within the output, except those rendered offscreen (thumbnails, window screencasts),
input method and lock screen windows. A marked window gets no frame callbacks with the output's
frames and its damage and commits schedule none (RenderView::scheduleRepaint); its repaints are
kept. A heartbeat sends it frame callbacks once a second, so that clients waiting for one
(eglSwapBuffers, FIFO) carry on slowly, and also notices a cover that changed without a frame. A
ping sends them at once, so that a client blocked in eglSwapBuffers answers in time. When the
cover goes, the next frame paints the windows below with their collected repaints and sends their
frame callbacks. Partly covered windows are not affected.

Similar upstream: draft MR !9732 (stop driving fully occluded windows, no low-rate callbacks);
Weston 14, wlroots, mutter send none to occluded surfaces; Smithay compositors about 1 Hz.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-03
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [generic: upstream draft !9732 goes further (any occlusion, no heartbeat); this one only the whole-output case]
X-Rungic-Tests: L1:testFullscreenOcclusion; L1:full suite against the earlier baseline; L3 by hand (docs/research/97 §20.1: renders per second with an animation behind the fullscreen floating window)
